In-Situ SOP Materials Inventory
.AU
Neural Motion
.DA
3 September 2026
.PP
This inventory covers the 10 SOPs currently listed in the In_Situ_SOPs folder. Quantities are per episode unless noted otherwise. Fixed installations are separated from reusable tools and consumable or input materials.
.NH 1
Materials by Task
.NH 2
1. Feed a Conveyor Line Station
.IP "Fixed equipment:" 18
Stub conveyor with running belt, evenly spaced white pitch marks, near and far rails, overhead light bar and conduit, entry and transfer flags, takt lamp, read-only count panel, fixed load shelf, and orientation nest with rib.
.IP "Reusable items:" 18
Parts tote and reject bin.
.IP "Inputs:" 18
10 square-based housing parts in the tote, plus 1 misfeed part pre-positioned on the belt. Confirm whether the misfeed is additional, making 11 parts total.
.NH 2
2. Grease a Machine Round
.IP "Fixed equipment:" 18
Stopped and isolated machine, lockout tag, 3 same-size grease zerks, guard shelf, frame rail, hose clip, tool shelf, fixed grease-gun cradle, and card holder.
.IP "Reusable items:" 18
Primed lever grease gun with hose and fitting coupler, blue wipe rag, red purge rag, and grease pencil.
.IP "Consumables:" 18
Grease sufficient for 9 full strokes (3 strokes at each of 3 zerks) and a lube card with at least 1 empty three-box row.
.NH 2
3. Load the Dishwasher
.IP "Fixed equipment:" 18
Installed dishwasher with working latch, open detergent dispenser, control panel, upper and lower racks, clipped cutlery basket, draining board, and utensil cup.
.IP "Inputs:" 18
2 plates, 2 bowls, 2 cups, 2 forks, 2 knives, 2 spoons, and 1 dishwasher detergent pod.
.NH 2
4. Mop a Floor Zone
.IP "Fixed equipment:" 18
Defined hard-floor bay with back kick rail, left and right plinth ends, and fixed mop rest.
.IP "Reusable items:" 18
Rectangular bucket with wringer and fill line, handled water jug, flat mop, fitted absorbent pad, and folding A-frame caution sign.
.IP "Consumables:" 18
Clean water measured to the bucket fill line and 1 clean, dry mop pad fitted to the mop.
.NH 2
5. Refill the Kettle and Dispenser at the Sink
.IP "Fixed equipment:" 18
Sink with working cold-water mixer tap, counter, kettle power base, and fixed dispenser body with jug cradle and drip tray.
.IP "Reusable items:" 18
Electric kettle, clear dispenser jug, and absorbent cloth.
.IP "Consumables:" 18
Cold tap water sufficient to fill both the partly filled kettle and partly filled dispenser jug to their marked fill lines.
.NH 2
6. Restock the Refrigerator In Situ
.IP "Fixed equipment:" 18
Installed refrigerator with open left-hinged door, working shelf, crisper drawer, tall and short door bins, and clear adjacent counter.
.IP "Reusable items:" 18
Stock tote.
.IP "Initial stock:" 18
1 older carton, 1 older jar, 1 older tub, 1 older produce pack, 1 older bottle, and 1 older small jar.
.IP "New stock:" 18
1 carton, 1 jar, 1 tub, 2 produce packs, 1 bottle, and 1 small jar (7 new items total).
.NH 2
7. Run a Microwave Heating Cycle
.IP "Fixed equipment:" 18
Installed microwave with turntable, front controls, working door and latch, and clear heat-proof counter.
.IP "Reusable items:" 18
Heat-proof plate with broad rim, vented dome cover with tab, food tub, and spoon.
.IP "Consumables:" 18
Thick prepared food sufficient for 3 level spoonfuls, with some food remaining in the tub.
.NH 2
8. Squeegee a Mirror Panel
.IP "Fixed equipment:" 18
Fixed framed mirror panel and clear counter with bottle, cloth, and squeegee positions.
.IP "Reusable items:" 18
Trigger spray bottle set to fan spray, straight rubber-blade squeegee, and absorbent lint-free cloth.
.IP "Consumables:" 18
Glass cleaner sufficient for at least 6 trigger bursts.
.NH 2
9. Tend a 3D Printer
.IP "Fixed equipment:" 18
Installed 3D printer with magnetic bed, locating pins, parked toolhead, working control panel, and plate rest or work area.
.IP "Reusable items:" 18
Flexible steel build plate, debris tray, stiff plastic scraper, and soft brush.
.IP "Inputs:" 18
1 completed printed part attached to the plate, with skirt and purge line, and 1 next print job ready in the printer queue.
.NH 2
10. Tidy a Bookshelf
.IP "Fixed equipment:" 18
Bookcase with working shelf, shelf above, fixed right end panel, and lower shelf.
.IP "Reusable items:" 18
Open bin, damp cleaning cloth, and solid freestanding bookend.
.IP "Inputs:" 18
6 books of visibly different heights; 1 mug, 1 small picture frame, and 1 coiled cable; and visible removable dust on the shelf lip.
.NH 1
Consolidated Episode Inputs and Consumables
.IP \(bu 4
Conveyor: 10 tote parts plus 1 belt misfeed part.
.IP \(bu 4
Greasing: grease for at least 9 strokes and 1 blank lube-card row.
.IP \(bu 4
Dishwasher: 12 place-setting items and 1 detergent pod.
.IP \(bu 4
Mopping: water to the bucket fill line and 1 clean mop pad.
.IP \(bu 4
Sink refill: cold water for the kettle and dispenser jug.
.IP \(bu 4
Refrigerator: 7 new stock items plus 6 older items for initial placement.
.IP \(bu 4
Microwave: food for 3 level spoonfuls plus remainder.
.IP \(bu 4
Mirror: glass cleaner for at least 6 bursts.
.IP \(bu 4
3D printer: 1 completed print with skirt and purge line, plus 1 queued job.
.IP \(bu 4
Bookshelf: 6 books, 3 non-book objects, and removable shelf dust.
.NH 1
Items to Confirm Before Procurement
.IP "1." 4
Conveyor part count: confirm whether to stage 11 total parts or take the belt misfeed from the original set of 10.
.IP "2." 4
Select and record repeatable specifications for food, glass cleaner, grease grade, mop-water additive, detergent pods, and book sizes.
.IP "3." 4
Define replacement frequency for rags, cloths, mop pads, lube cards, detergent pods, food, printed parts, and simulated refrigerator stock.
.IP "4." 4
Confirm the authorized lockout procedure and responsible person for the grease task.
.PP
Scope note: the program status report references 59 planned in-situ tasks, but only 10 in-situ SOPs are currently present in the folder. This inventory covers those 10 available SOPs.
